{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793381497,"nonce":"112zUUZFvXGeL2T0+W9VdPavOSA=","message":"Capture is now streaming: render thread reads back into a pooled buffer (driver readback into a reused Pixels, no per-frame allocation) and publishes to a latest-wins slot; a sender thread diffs rows with a native compare, writes, and recycles buffers. Viewer side: records are parsed and inflated before taking the feed lock; the lock covers copies only. Per frame at 640x360 on this Mac: render 1.2 ms, readback 0.8, diff 0.6, write 0.2 (SURFACE_STATS=1); 4 of 244 frames dropped by the slot early in the run. The earlier lag was the Haxe per-pixel diff on the render thread, not the readback. Not asynchronous: hlsdl exposes only synchronous readPixels (no pixel buffers or fences), so the readback itself blocks the render thread for the GPU round trip; a pixel-buffer path needs hlsdl/ashui native support. Still unmeasured: input-to-frame latency in the tab and the cost at 1280x720.","files":null}]}